(LIB-39 -- a bare `Return <expr>.`, with no `a <type>,` clause, records
 no return type at all in the .lib -- not even a list's element type --
 unlike `Return a list, out.`, which LIB-listinfer.vox shows does record
 one. See also Discrepancy 3: a caller of `five` below can still assign
 its result to a typed variable with no diagnostic, even though the .lib
 says it returns nothing.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox
   docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-barereturn.vox --shared -o barereturn.so
   cat barereturn.lib
 expected output: exit 0, and barereturn.lib reads:
   Library barekit version "1.0".
   Location "./barereturn.so".

   Table of Contents:
       To five with a number called x.
       To 'echo list bare' with a list called items.
)

Library barekit version "1.0".

To five with a number called x. Return x add 1.

To 'echo list bare' with a list called items.
  Return items.
